# Patch 003 — Mempool ancestor/descendant accounting cleanup
#
# Target base: eCash v0.24.11  fa7a44f731a2dfe1587e572d9eb0e4bb7c73d79c
#
# Status: DEFERRED — this patch is a NO-OP when applied during the
#         rebase to bitcoin-abc 252182e9.
#
# Background
# ----------
# eCash v0.24.11 (and Bitcoin) maintains per-entry ancestor/descendant
# accounting fields in CTxMemPoolEntry:
#
#   nCountWithAncestors, nSizeWithAncestors, nModFeesWithAncestors,
#   nSigOpCountWithAncestors, nCountWithDescendants, nSizeWithDescendants,
#   nModFeesWithDescendants, nSigOpCountWithDescendants
#
# These fields are kept up-to-date by O(n²) maintenance functions:
#   UpdateAncestorsOf, UpdateEntryForAncestors, UpdateChildrenForRemoval,
#   UpdateForRemoveFromMempool, UpdateDescendantsFromParent
#
# The original O(n²) mining algorithm (addPackageTxs) used these fields to
# evaluate package fee rates during block construction.  After patch 001
# replaced mining with an O(n log n) algorithm that takes a one-shot snapshot
# and computes package stats inline, these per-entry fields are only consulted
# for two purposes:
#
#   1. CalculateMemPoolAncestors limit enforcement  → removed by patch 002
#   2. ancestor_score / descendant_score sort indices in the multi-index map
#      → only used internally by TrimToSize and the old mining algorithm
#
# Removing them eliminates an O(n²) cost on every mempool insertion and
# reduces CTxMemPoolEntry size by ~56 bytes.
#
# Plan (to be executed during the bitcoin-abc 252182e9 rebase)
# -----------------------------------------------------------
# bitcoin-abc upstream already removed this entire subsystem before 252182e9.
# When the v1 series is rebased onto 252182e9, all conflicts in these areas
# will be resolved by accepting the upstream removal.  This patch file
# documents the intent; no diff hunks are needed because the target state
# is already the bitcoin-abc HEAD state.
#
# If for any reason the v1 series must be built on top of eCash v0.24.11
# without first rebasing to 252182e9, apply the following changes manually:
#
#  src/txmempool.h
#   - Remove CTxMemPoolModifiedEntry struct
#   - Remove nCountWithAncestors / nSizeWithAncestors / nModFeesWithAncestors /
#     nSigOpCountWithAncestors fields from CTxMemPoolEntry
#   - Remove nCountWithDescendants / nSizeWithDescendants /
#     nModFeesWithDescendants / nSigOpCountWithDescendants fields
#   - Remove GetCountWithAncestors / GetSizeWithAncestors /
#     GetModFeesWithAncestors / GetVirtualSizeWithAncestors /
#     GetCountWithDescendants / GetSizeWithDescendants /
#     GetModFeesWithDescendants accessors
#   - Remove update_descendant_state / update_ancestor_state functors
#   - Remove ancestor_score / descendant_score multi-index tags and indices
#
#  src/txmempool.cpp
#   - Remove UpdateAncestorsOf, UpdateEntryForAncestors,
#     UpdateChildrenForRemoval, UpdateForRemoveFromMempool,
#     UpdateDescendantsFromParent implementations
#   - Remove their calls in addUnchecked, removeUnchecked, etc.
#
#  src/txmempool.h (CalculateMemPoolAncestors)
#   - Remove limitAncestorCount / limitAncestorSize / limitDescendantCount /
#     limitDescendantSize parameters (all callers already pass nNoLimit after
#     patch 002; simplify signature to remove limit params entirely)
#
# No diff is present in this file; the rebase resolves it automatically.
